  - exact certificates
abstract: >-
  Exhaustive enumeration of all connected graphs on up to eleven vertices —
  1006700565 of them at the last size — by the contextuality gap
  Delta(G) = theta(G) - alpha(G). The largest gap at each size is identified by that
  sweep, and for every graph so identified the Lovasz theta number is established by
  machine-checked primal and dual certificates in exact arithmetic: a closed form
  where one exists, and a certified rational interval where none does. The value of
  each named maximizer is proved; that it is the maximum over all graphs of its size
  rests on the sweep's numerics and is not. The eight-vertex value, left open by the
  paper this continues, is the root of x^4 - x^3 + 23x^2 - 155x + 158 in the interval
  (3, 4); its Galois group is the full symmetric group on four letters, so the degree
  cannot be reduced.
